@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.security"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Account Partner Worker Permissions
	Testing to assure that provisioning partner account worker permissions works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a provisioning user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | provisioning.worker                    |
	| Email Address | provisioning.worker@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Provisioning                           |
	| Last Name     | Worker                                 |
	* I assign the provisioning user with the email address "provisioning.worker@liferay.com.broken" to the provisioning role "Provisioning Worker"
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prm.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRM                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prm.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRM                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Misper - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Perpar - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Permission Partner |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| PERPARPERPAR |
	| MISPERPERMIS |
	| MISPER       |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Perpar - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| PERPARPERPAR |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| MISPERPERMIS |
	| MISPER       |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Perpar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from provisioning
	| provisioning.worker@liferay.com.broken |

Scenario: Add partner
	Testing the ability to create a T4 project in Dossiera and add the project partner in the provisioning page account details 

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRM                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRM                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | PERPARPERPAR                                   | |
	| Contact Email Address | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken           | |
	| Description           | Test provisioning partner account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-9012                                   | |
	| Name                  | Perpar - ${staticProjectName}                  | |
	| Profile Email Address | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken           | |
	| Region                | United States                                  | |
	| Status                | Active                                         | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                             | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikipartner.com                       | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Perpar - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Perpetual   | true     | |
	| Quantity    | 1        | |
	| Status      | Approved | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.worker@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Details" tab
	And I edit the following account fields and types to the following values under the account details tab
	| Partner/Reseller/SI | Select Entity | Perpar - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| First Line Support  | Select Entity | Perpar - ${staticProjectName} | |
	Then I should be able to view the following account values in the account details page
	| Name           | Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code           | MISPERPERMIS                  |
	| State          | ACTIVE                        |
	| Support Region | United States                 |
	| Country        | United States                 |
	| SLA            | Platinum                      |
	| Support Seats  | 1 / 3 Filled                  |
	| Tier           | T4                            |
	| FLS Partner    | Perpar - ${staticProjectName} |
	Then I should be able to view the following account values under the account details tab
	| Account Name        | Permis - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| State               | ACTIVE                        | |
	| Code                | MISPERPERMIS                  | |
	| Tier                | T4                            | |
	| Data Region         | United States                 | |
	| Partner/Reseller/SI | Perpar - ${staticProjectName} |	|
	| First Line Support  | Perpar - ${staticProjectName} |	|
	| Street 1            | 456 Fake Street               | |
	| Country             | United States                 | |
	| City                | Diamond Bar                   | |
	| State/Province      | California                    | |
	| Postal Code         | 91765                         | |
	| Primary             | true                          | |
	| Dossiera Project    | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}   | |
	| Salesforce Project  | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} | |
	And the team with the name "Perpar - ${staticProjectName}" assigned the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" should have the team role "Partner"
	And the team with the name "Perpar - ${staticProjectName}" assigned the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" should have the team role "First Line Support"
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the partner link in the account header
	Then I should be able to view the following team values in the team details page
	| Name | Perpar - ${staticProjectName} |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Perpar"
	And I click on the account with the name "Perpar - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Teams" tab
	Then I should be able to view the team with the name "Perpar - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name                         | Perpar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Partner/Reseller/SI Accounts | 1                             |
	| First Line Support Accounts  | 1                             |
	When I click on the "Perpar - ${staticProjectName}" team link
	And I click on the "Partner/Reseller/SI Accounts" tab
	Then I should be able to view an account on the team details page with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Account Name  | Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code          | MISPERPERMIS                  |
	| Region        | United States                 |
	| SLA           | Platinum                      |
	| Tier          | T4                            |
	| Account State | ACTIVE                        |
	When I click on the "First Line Support Accounts" tab
	Then I should be able to view an account on the team details page with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Account Name  | Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code          | MISPERPERMIS                  |
	| Region        | United States                 |
	| SLA           | Platinum                      |
	| Tier          | T4                            |
	| Account State | ACTIVE                        |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	Then I should be able to view an account on the provisioning index with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name    | Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code    | MISPERPERMIS                  |
	| Partner | Perpar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Region  | United States                 |
	| SLA     | Platinum                      |
	| Tier    | T4                            |
	| State   | ACTIVE                        |
	When I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "History" tab
	And I generate the account ID value for "Permis - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "contactEmailAddress" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account                 |
	| Update Field Name           | contactEmailAddress                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "internal" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | internal             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | false                |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "code" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | code                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | MISPERPERMIS         |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "region" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | region               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | United States        |
	And I generate the account ID value for "Misper - ${staticCompanyName}"
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "parentAccountId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | parentAccountId      |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}   |
	And I generate the account ID value for "Permis - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "accountId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId            |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}   |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "name" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account          |
	| Update Field Name           | name                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "status" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | status               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | Active               |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Account" with the field value "tier" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | tier                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | T4                   |
	And the history entry number "1" with the keyword "Provisioning Worker > Assigned Team" with the field value "Team Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Worker > Assigned Team > Perpar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Update Field Name           | Team Role                                                           |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                                 |
	| Update Field New Value      | Partner                                                             |
	And the history entry number "2" with the keyword "Provisioning Worker > Assigned Team" with the field value "Team Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Worker > Assigned Team > Perpar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Update Field Name           | Team Role                                                           |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                                 |
	| Update Field New Value      | First Line Support                                                  |

